---
import RouteShell from "../../../components/RouteShell.astro";
export const prerender = true;
const url = "https://www.miamiknifeguy.com/learn/miami-knife-sharpening-pickup-cost/";
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: "What Does Knife Sharpening Pickup Cost in Miami?", datePublished: "2026-10-03", dateModified: "2026-10-03", author: { "@id": "https://www.miamiknifeguy.com/#business" }, publisher: { "@id": "https://www.miamiknifeguy.com/#business" }, mainEntityOfPage: url };
---
<RouteShell title="Miami Knife Sharpening Pickup Cost | Miami Knife Guy" description="Miami Knife Guy charges for sharpening work and pickup travel separately. Pickup and return cost $1 per total driven mile for any knife count; Sean confirms mileage before scheduling." canonicalPath="/learn/miami-knife-sharpening-pickup-cost/" schema={schema}>
  <main class="panel" aria-hidden="false"><article class="panel-inner max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <nav class="intake-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/learn/">← Knife care articles</a></nav>
    <p class="sub-eyebrow">Local service · Updated October 3, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="sub-headline-cyan text-4xl lg:text-5xl mb-6">What does knife sharpening pickup cost in Miami?</h1>
    <p class="sub-body mb-8">Pickup and return cost <strong class="text-white">$1 per total driven mile, for any number of knives</strong>. Sharpening and repairs are priced separately by the work. Sean confirms route mileage and the travel charge before scheduling.</p>
    <div class="space-y-8 text-white/80 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <section><h2 class="text-white text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">How is the travel charge calculated?</h2><p>Add the miles driven for the complete pickup and return route, then multiply by $1. For an illustrative 18-mile total route, the travel charge would be $18. This is an example, not a quote for a specific address. The confirmed route may differ.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-white text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Does the knife count change that rate?</h2><p>No. The published travel rate applies across any knife count. The number, type, and condition of knives affect the sharpening or repair quote, not the $1-per-mile travel rule.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-white text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Can I avoid a travel charge?</h2><p>Shop drop-off is the leanest handoff for local home knives. If pickup and return are more convenient, request them on the local service form and provide your location. Sean will confirm whether the route and timing work.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-white text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">What information should I send?</h2><p>Share your city or address, knife count, blade types, visible damage, and timing. Photos can help with unusual work; the final quote depends on inspection. If you are outside the local area, <a class="text-cyan-300 underline" href="/book/mail-in/">start a mail-in request</a> before shipping.</p></section>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-10"><a class="panel-cta-btn panel-cta-cyan" href="/book/home/?intent=one-time">Request One-Time Sharpening</a><a class="panel-cta-btn panel-cta-ghost" href="/services/">View Prices</a></div>
  </article></main>
</RouteShell>
